{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md at exact 5e56197310ff5adca0ce6c530def60c961f1999a on request/lane-worktree-identity (pushed; one commit over main d1ae6ade; documentation only), a design candidate under promise 4014b84e on request 0aeb7270 (#20819), stage one of the adopted lane and worktree identity outcome of #13177. It restates the four adopted layers of the 2026-08-27 design (artifact 953c3746 at 6131249c, adopted by proposal cb755aa1 ratified 986a1ca2) over current source at d1ae6ade: layer 1, a bounded read-only reverse association from implementing-commit Rests-On facts and actual refs and worktrees to durable work, reusing the hardened NUL-framed trailer scan with object re-verification, the checkout inventory and its cache and cap, the shared step budget and canonical event resolution with typed refusals; layer 2, guarded worktree creation and stamping with a private per-checkout record, a commit message template and an opt-in narrow hook, warning and asking when the governing lane settles; layer 3, deterministic lane refs under refs/gitseq/lanes keyed by governing record and attempt, allocated by compare-and-swap, surviving checkout removal, with human branch aliases; layer 4, validated branch display fields that grant no authority, noting that requests already carry the validated target_ref. It separates claimed identity from verified durable evidence, local location and actual permission: the kernel's envelope trailer is signed and verified byte for byte, an implementing commit's Rests-On is unsigned prose read for display, and neither a trailer, a ref, a config value nor a path grants signing or filesystem authority; a shared head or an expired lease alone never makes a tree removable. It gives cleanup-candidate, duplicate-checkout, refless-head and scratch-tree behaviour, read-only inventory with no writes, refusal before signing or unsafe mutation, and a proof-obligation table covering every condition the request names. This head implements nothing and closes nothing: no gs worktree command, per-checkout record or lane ref exists at it; no gate beyond go build and diff-check applies to two notes. New path; no live artifact at it. The adopted note's path is not in main, so there is no in-target predecessor; 953c3746 is cited as the design this reconciles.","body":{"branch":"request/lane-worktree-identity","commit":"5e56197310ff5adca0ce6c530def60c961f1999a","path":"notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4a12a00134069b072cf782934b5380e64014b84e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0aeb727057a5b3b2b3642be8c70cde7c63865d1e"}}